 "prompt": "Solve the following problem as completely as you can.\n\n<problem>\nFor $N\\in\\mathbb N$ let $r_3(N)$ denote the largest size of a set $A\\subseteq[N]=\\{1,\\dots,N\\}$ containing no non-trivial $3$-term arithmetic progression, i.e. no $x,x+d,x+2d\\in A$ with $d\\neq0$. Behrend's construction gives $r_3(N)\\ge N\\exp\\big(-(c_B+o(1))\\sqrt{\\log N}\\big)$ with $c_B=2\\sqrt{2\\log 2}\\approx 2.355$, and no construction has improved this constant. Define\n$$\\kappa=\\liminf_{N\\to\\infty}\\frac{\\log\\big(N/r_3(N)\\big)}{\\sqrt{\\log N}}\\in[0,c_B].$$\nProblem. Construct an infinite family of $3$-AP-free sets $A_N\\subseteq[N]$ with $|A_N|\\ge N\\exp(-c\\sqrt{\\log N})$ for some constant $c<2\\sqrt{2\\log 2}$, thereby showing $\\kappa<c_B$. More ambitiously: is $\\kappa=0$, i.e. are there $3$-AP-free sets with $|A_N|\\ge N\\exp(-(\\log N)^{\\gamma})$ for some fixed $\\gamma<1/2$ and infinitely many $N$?\n</problem>\n\n<finite_instance>\nFind a set $A\\subseteq\\{1,2,\\dots,20000\\}$ with $|A|\\ge1300$ containing no three distinct elements $x<y<z$ with $x+z=2y$. (For comparison: the digit construction with base-$3$ digits in $\\{0,1\\}$ gives about $520$ elements, the product of exact extremal sets for $[123]$ and $[81]$ gives $32\\cdot24=768$ elements in $[19926]$, and extrapolating the known exact values $r_3(N)$ for $N\\le123$ with the empirical local growth exponent $\\approx0.70$–$0.75$ places $r_3(20000)$ somewhere around $1100$–$1500$; $1300$ is believed to be beyond any published or easily searched construction.)\n</finite_instance>\n\n<required_candidate_format>\nA JSON array of at least 1300 distinct integers, each between 1 and 20000 inclusive (order irrelevant).\n</required_candidate_format>\n\nReturn\n- text: your full solution or best partial progress: definitions, the argument, and a clear final answer. If you cannot solve it, state exactly what you proved and what remains.\n- claimed_status: \"solved\" only if you believe the problem (or, when given, the finite instance) is fully solved; \"partial\" for real progress; \"unsolved\" otherwise.\n- candidate: if a finite instance is given, the object you propose, exactly in the required JSON shape; otherwise null.\n",
